IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`
IMPORT `sgba-sched`
IMPORT `sgba-p1-online`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 1: section 2(1), the defined terms, in the Act's own (alphabetical) order.
-- Pattern. A term the Act defines with "means" is a function from the facts that make something fall within it to
-- a BOOLEAN. A term it defines with "includes" is a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE when the thing is one the Act lists,
-- NOTHING when the definition does not say (an inclusive definition never excludes). Where the Act's definition
-- points at another provision, the function calls that provision's rule or, for a forward reference, takes its result as a fact.
-- Terms that depend on the Schedules take the date and answer NOTHING outside the window of the deposited text.

§ `2(1) Interpretation: the defined terms`

-- src:251 | “a point” includes a mobile or potentially mobile point, whether
-- src:252 | on land, underground, in the atmosphere, underwater or
-- src:253 | anywhere else;
@ref s 2(1) "a point" (src:251-253)
GIVEN `it is a mobile or potentially mobile point` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) a point includes this mobile or potentially mobile point, wherever it is` MEANS
    IF `it is a mobile or potentially mobile point` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:257 | “access”, in relation to any content, means to read, view, hear or
-- src:258 | otherwise experience content, by means of a broadcasting
-- src:259 | service or an electronic service, and includes —
@ref s 2(1) "access" (means) (src:257-259)
GIVEN `the person reads, views, hears or otherwise experiences content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by means of a broadcasting service or an electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person has access to the content` MEANS
    `the person reads, views, hears or otherwise experiences content` AND `by means of a broadcasting service or an electronic service`

-- src:259 | service or an electronic service, and includes —
-- src:261 | (a) access that is subject to a precondition, such as the
-- src:262 | use of a password;
-- src:264 | (b) access by way of push technology;
-- src:266 | (c) access by way of a standing request; and
-- src:268 | (d) access for a limited period of time only;
@ref s 2(1) "access" (includes (a) to (d)) (src:259-268)
GIVEN `the access is subject to a precondition such as the use of a password` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the access is by way of push technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the access is by way of a standing request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the access is for a limited period of time only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) access includes this kind of access` MEANS
    IF `the access is subject to a precondition such as the use of a password` OR `the access is by way of push technology` OR `the access is by way of a standing request` OR `the access is for a limited period of time only`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:272 | “Authority” means the Info-communications Media
-- src:273 | Development Authority established by section 3 of the
-- src:274 | Info‑communications Media Development Authority
-- src:275 | Act 2016;
@ref s 2(1) "Authority" (src:272-275)
GIVEN `it is the Info-communications Media Development Authority established by section 3 of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the body is the Authority` MEANS
    `it is the Info-communications Media Development Authority established by section 3 of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016`

-- src:277 | “broadcasting apparatus” means any apparatus capable of or
-- src:278 | designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting
-- src:279 | service and specified in the First Schedule;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus" (src:277-279)
-- Dated: it depends on the First Schedule. NOTHING outside the window of the deposited text.
-- READING (fork F-BA-01): "any apparatus capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting service and specified in the First Schedule"
-- is read with "specified in the First Schedule" qualifying the whole of "apparatus capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting service" (reading A).
-- The other reading attaches "specified in the First Schedule" only to "designed or constructed for" (reading B); NOTES.md sets out both and the text for each.
-- The input fact `capable of reception of a broadcasting service` stands for "capable of, or designed or constructed for, the reception of any broadcasting service".
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      a IS A Apparatus
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the apparatus is broadcasting apparatus on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` d a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST listed THEN JUST (a's `capable of reception of a broadcasting service` AND listed)

-- src:281 | “broadcasting apparatus licence” means a licence granted under
-- src:282 | section 20 in respect of broadcasting apparatus, and
-- src:283 | “broadcasting apparatus licensee” is to be construed
-- src:284 | accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus licence" and "broadcasting apparatus licensee" (src:281-284)
GIVEN `it is a licence granted under section 20 in respect of broadcasting apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the licence is a broadcasting apparatus licence` MEANS
    `it is a licence granted under section 20 in respect of broadcasting apparatus`

-- src:283 | “broadcasting apparatus licensee” is to be construed
-- src:284 | accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus licensee" (src:283-284)
GIVEN `it holds a broadcasting apparatus licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is a broadcasting apparatus licensee` MEANS
    `it holds a broadcasting apparatus licence`

-- src:286 | “broadcasting licence” means a licence granted under section 8
-- src:287 | or 9 for the provision of a licensable broadcasting service,
-- src:288 | and “broadcasting licensee” is to be construed accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting licence" and "broadcasting licensee" (src:286-288)
GIVEN `it is a licence granted under section 8 or 9 for the provision of a licensable broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the licence is a broadcasting licence` MEANS
    `it is a licence granted under section 8 or 9 for the provision of a licensable broadcasting service`

-- src:288 | and “broadcasting licensee” is to be construed accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting licensee" (src:288)
GIVEN `it holds a broadcasting licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is a broadcasting licensee` MEANS
    `it holds a broadcasting licence`

-- src:290 | “broadcasting service” means a service whereby signs or signals
-- src:291 | transmitted (whether or not encrypted) comprise —
-- src:296 | (a) any programme capable of being received, or
-- src:297 | received and displayed, as visual images, whether
-- src:298 | moving or still;
-- src:300 | (b) any sound programme for reception; or
-- src:302 | (c) any programme, being a combination of both visual
-- src:303 | image (whether moving or still) and sound for
-- src:304 | reception or reception and display,
-- src:306 | by persons having equipment appropriate for receiving or
-- src:307 | receiving and displaying (as the case may be) that service,
-- src:308 | irrespective of the means of delivery of that service;
@ref s 2(1) "broadcasting service" (src:290-308)
GIVEN `signs or signals are transmitted, whether or not encrypted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they comprise a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they comprise a sound programme for reception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they comprise a programme that combines visual images and sound for reception or reception and display` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving or receiving and displaying that service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is a broadcasting service` MEANS
    `signs or signals are transmitted, whether or not encrypted`
    AND `the service is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving or receiving and displaying that service`
    AND (`they comprise a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images` OR `they comprise a sound programme for reception` OR `they comprise a programme that combines visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`)

-- src:310 | “Chief Executive”, in relation to the Authority, means the Chief
-- src:311 | Executive of the Authority appointed under section 40(1) of
-- src:312 | the Info-communications Media Development Authority
-- src:313 | Act 2016, and includes any individual acting in that capacity;
@ref s 2(1) "Chief Executive" (src:310-313)
GIVEN `it is the Chief Executive of the Authority appointed under section 40(1) of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an individual acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is the Chief Executive in relation to the Authority` MEANS
    `it is the Chief Executive of the Authority appointed under section 40(1) of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016` OR `it is an individual acting in that capacity`

-- src:315 | “class licence” means a licence determined under section 9 to be
-- src:316 | applicable to certain licensable broadcasting services, and
-- src:317 | “class licensee” is to be construed accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "class licence" (src:315-317)
GIVEN `it is a licence determined under section 9 to be applicable to certain licensable broadcasting services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the licence is a class licence` MEANS
    `it is a licence determined under section 9 to be applicable to certain licensable broadcasting services`

-- src:317 | “class licensee” is to be construed accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "class licensee" (src:317)
GIVEN `a class licence applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is a class licensee` MEANS
    `a class licence applies to the person`

-- src:319 | “Code of Practice” means a Code of Practice issued under this
-- src:320 | Act;
@ref s 2(1) "Code of Practice" (src:319-320)
GIVEN `it is a Code of Practice issued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the document is a Code of Practice` MEANS
    `it is a Code of Practice issued under this Act`

-- src:322 | “communicate”, in relation to any content, means —
-- src:324 | (a) to make available (by posting or otherwise); or
-- src:326 | (b) to distribute (by sharing or forwarding or otherwise),
-- src:328 | the content, regardless if the communication is between
-- src:329 | persons and persons, things and things or persons and things;
@ref s 2(1) "communicate" (src:322-329)
GIVEN `the content is made available, by posting or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the content is distributed, by sharing or forwarding or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person communicates the content` MEANS
    `the content is made available, by posting or otherwise` OR `the content is distributed, by sharing or forwarding or otherwise`

-- src:333 | “content” means information or material capable of
-- src:334 | communication by means of a broadcasting service or an
-- src:335 | electronic service —
-- src:337 | (a) whether in the form of text;
-- src:339 | (b) whether in the form of speech, music or other sounds;
-- src:341 | (c) whether in the form of visual images (animated or
-- src:342 | otherwise), pictorial or graphic form (for example, an
-- src:343 | anthropomorphic or a humanlike depiction);
-- src:348 | (d) whether in any other form; or
-- src:350 | (e) whether in any combination of forms;
@ref s 2(1) "content" (src:333-350)
GIVEN `it is information or material capable of communication by means of a broadcasting service or an electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the information or material is content, in whatever form (text, speech, music or other sounds, visual images, any other form, or any combination)` MEANS
    `it is information or material capable of communication by means of a broadcasting service or an electronic service`

-- src:354 | “debenture” includes debenture stock;
@ref s 2(1) "debenture" (src:354)
GIVEN `it is debenture stock` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) debenture includes this debenture stock` MEANS
    IF `it is debenture stock` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:356 | “dwelling house” includes a hotel, inn, boarding house or other
-- src:357 | similar establishment;
@ref s 2(1) "dwelling house" (src:356-357)
GIVEN `it is a hotel, inn, boarding house or other similar establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) dwelling house includes this establishment` MEANS
    IF `it is a hotel, inn, boarding house or other similar establishment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:359 | “electronic service” has the meaning given by section 2A(2);
@ref s 2(1) "electronic service" (src:359)
-- The meaning is in s 2A(2); the function is the same rule.
GIVEN `the service meets section 2A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is an electronic service as section 2A(2) gives the meaning` MEANS
    `the service meets section 2A(2)`

-- src:363 | “encrypted” means treated electronically or otherwise to prevent
-- src:364 | intelligible reception;
@ref s 2(1) "encrypted" (src:363-364)
GIVEN `it is treated electronically or otherwise to prevent intelligible reception` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the transmission is encrypted` MEANS
    `it is treated electronically or otherwise to prevent intelligible reception`

-- src:366 | “end-user”, in relation to an electronic service, means an
-- src:367 | individual who, or an entity that, and whether or not in the
-- src:368 | course of business —
-- src:370 | (a) has access to content or something which contains
-- src:371 | content; or
-- src:373 | (b) communicates content, or something which contains
-- src:374 | content,
-- src:376 | on or by means of the electronic service, but excludes a
-- src:377 | person who is prescribed by the Minister by order in the
-- src:378 | Gazette;
@ref s 2(1) "end-user" (src:366-378)
GIVEN `it is an individual or an entity, whether or not in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has access to content or something which contains content, on or by means of the electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it communicates content or something which contains content, on or by means of the electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person the Minister has prescribed by order in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is an end-user of the electronic service` MEANS
    `it is an individual or an entity, whether or not in the course of business`
    AND (`it has access to content or something which contains content, on or by means of the electronic service` OR `it communicates content or something which contains content, on or by means of the electronic service`)
    AND (NOT `it is a person the Minister has prescribed by order in the Gazette`)

-- src:382 | “engage in conduct” means —
-- src:384 | (a) to do an act or omit to do an act —
-- src:386 | (i) on a single occasion; or
-- src:388 | (ii) on a number of occasions over a period of time;
-- src:389 | or
-- src:391 | (b) to both do an act and omit to do an act —
-- src:393 | (i) on a single occasion; or
-- src:395 | (ii) on a number of occasions over a period of time;
@ref s 2(1) "engage in conduct" (src:382-395)
GIVEN `it does an act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it omits to do an act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person engages in conduct, on a single occasion or on a number of occasions over a period of time` MEANS
    `it does an act` OR `it omits to do an act`

-- src:402 | “entity” means —
-- src:404 | (a) a body corporate (including a limited liability
-- src:405 | partnership);
-- src:407 | (b) an unincorporated association;
-- src:409 | (c) a partnership;
-- src:411 | (d) a body politic;
-- src:413 | (e) a body of individuals who together form a body; or
-- src:415 | (f) a person other than an individual;
@ref s 2(1) "entity" (src:402-415)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of person`
      `it is a body politic` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a body of individuals who together form a body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is an entity` MEANS
    `it is a body politic`
    OR `it is a body of individuals who together form a body`
    OR (CONSIDER k
        WHEN `an individual` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a body corporate` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an unincorporated association other than a partnership` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a partnership` THEN TRUE)

-- src:419 | “excluded electronic service” has the meaning given by
-- src:420 | section 2A(3);
@ref s 2(1) "excluded electronic service" (src:419-420)
-- The meaning is in s 2A(3); the function is the same rule.
GIVEN `the service is an excluded electronic service under section 2A(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is an excluded electronic service as section 2A(3) gives the meaning` MEANS
    `the service is an excluded electronic service under section 2A(3)`

-- src:424 | “free-to-air broadcasting service” means a licensable
-- src:425 | broadcasting service made available for reception in at
-- src:426 | least 2 dwelling houses by broadcasting apparatus commonly
-- src:427 | available to the public without payment of a subscription fee;
@ref s 2(1) "free-to-air broadcasting service" (src:424-427)
GIVEN `it is a licensable broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of dwelling houses in which it is made available for reception by broadcasting apparatus commonly available to the public` IS A NUMBER
      `a subscription fee is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is a free-to-air broadcasting service` MEANS
    `it is a licensable broadcasting service`
    AND `the number of dwelling houses in which it is made available for reception by broadcasting apparatus commonly available to the public` AT LEAST 2
    AND (NOT `a subscription fee is payable`)

-- src:429 | “free-to-air licence” means a broadcasting licence granted under
-- src:430 | this Act for the operation of a free-to-air broadcasting
-- src:431 | service, and “free-to-air licensee” is to be construed
-- src:432 | accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "free-to-air licence" and "free-to-air licensee" (src:429-432)
GIVEN `it is a broadcasting licence granted under this Act for the operation of a free-to-air broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the licence is a free-to-air licence` MEANS
    `it is a broadcasting licence granted under this Act for the operation of a free-to-air broadcasting service`

-- src:434 | “internet access service” means a telecommunication service
-- src:435 | between a point in Singapore and another point in Singapore
-- src:436 | or between 2 points, one of which is in Singapore —
-- src:438 | (a) that —
-- src:440 | (i) enables end-users to access content on the
-- src:441 | Internet using that service; or
-- src:443 | (ii) delivers content to persons having equipment
-- src:444 | appropriate for receiving that content on the
-- src:445 | Internet, where the delivery of the service is by
-- src:446 | a telecommunication service described in
-- src:447 | sub‑paragraph (i); and
-- src:449 | (b) that is covered by a licence under the
-- src:450 | Telecommunications Act 1999,
-- src:455 | but excludes a social media service and any
-- src:456 | telecommunication service prescribed by the Minister by
-- src:457 | order in the Gazette as excluded from this definition;
@ref s 2(1) "internet access service" (src:434-457)
GIVEN `it is a telecommunication service between a point in Singapore and another point in Singapore, or between 2 points one of which is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it enables end-users to access content on the Internet using that service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it delivers content to persons with equipment appropriate for receiving it on the Internet, the delivery being by a service of the first kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is covered by a licence under the Telecommunications Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a social media service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a telecommunication service the Minister has prescribed by order in the Gazette as excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is an internet access service` MEANS
    `it is a telecommunication service between a point in Singapore and another point in Singapore, or between 2 points one of which is in Singapore`
    AND (`it enables end-users to access content on the Internet using that service` OR `it delivers content to persons with equipment appropriate for receiving it on the Internet, the delivery being by a service of the first kind`)
    AND `it is covered by a licence under the Telecommunications Act 1999`
    AND (NOT `it is a social media service`)
    AND (NOT `it is a telecommunication service the Minister has prescribed by order in the Gazette as excluded`)

-- src:461 | “licence” means a licence granted under any provision of this
-- src:462 | Act, and “licensee” is to be construed accordingly;
@ref s 2(1) "licence" and "licensee" (src:461-462)
GIVEN `it is a licence granted under any provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the licence is a licence` MEANS
    `it is a licence granted under any provision of this Act`

-- src:464 | “licensable broadcasting service” means any broadcasting
-- src:465 | service specified in the Second Schedule and is not and has
-- src:466 | never been an online communication service;
@ref s 2(1) "licensable broadcasting service" (src:464-466)
-- The Second Schedule decides the first limb. NOTHING outside the window of the deposited text.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A MAYBE `Second Schedule service`
      `it is or has ever been an online communication service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the broadcasting service is a licensable broadcasting service on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the service is specified in the Second Schedule on` d s
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST listed THEN JUST (listed AND (NOT `it is or has ever been an online communication service`))

-- src:470 | “member” means a member of the Authority;
@ref s 2(1) "member" (src:470)
GIVEN `it is a member of the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the person is a member` MEANS
    `it is a member of the Authority`

-- src:472 | “online Code of Practice” means a Code of Practice that is issued
-- src:473 | or amended under section 45L or amended under
-- src:474 | section 59(3) on appeal;
@ref s 2(1) "online Code of Practice" (src:472-474)
GIVEN `it is a Code of Practice issued or amended under section 45L` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Code of Practice amended under section 59(3) on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the Code of Practice is an online Code of Practice` MEANS
    `it is a Code of Practice issued or amended under section 45L` OR `it is a Code of Practice amended under section 59(3) on appeal`

-- src:478 | “online communication service” has the meaning given by
-- src:479 | section 2A(1);
@ref s 2(1) "online communication service" (src:478-479)
-- The meaning is in s 2A(1).
GIVEN `the service is an online communication service under section 2A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is an online communication service as section 2A(1) gives the meaning` MEANS
    `the service is an online communication service under section 2A(1)`

-- src:483 | “Part 10A regulations” means regulations made under
-- src:484 | section 45P;
@ref s 2(1) "Part 10A regulations" (src:483-484)
GIVEN `they are regulations made under section 45P` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the regulations are Part 10A regulations` MEANS
    `they are regulations made under section 45P`

-- src:488 | “programme”, in relation to a broadcasting service, means —
-- src:490 | (a) any matter the primary purpose of which is to
-- src:491 | entertain, educate or inform all or part of the
-- src:492 | public; or
-- src:494 | (b) any advertising or sponsorship matter, whether or not
-- src:495 | of a commercial kind,
-- src:497 | but does not include any matter that is wholly related to or
-- src:498 | connected with any private communication, that is to say —
-- src:500 | (c) any communication between 2 or more persons that
-- src:501 | is of a private or domestic nature;
-- src:503 | (d) any internal communication of a business,
-- src:504 | Government agency or other organisation for the
-- src:509 | purpose of the operation of the business, agency or
-- src:510 | organisation; and
-- src:512 | (e) communications in such other circumstances as may
-- src:513 | be prescribed;
@ref s 2(1) "programme" (src:488-513)
GIVEN `its primary purpose is to entertain, educate or inform all or part of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is advertising or sponsorship matter, whether or not of a commercial kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is wholly related to or connected with a communication between 2 or more persons that is of a private or domestic nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is wholly related to or connected with an internal communication of a business, Government agency or other organisation for the purpose of its operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is wholly related to or connected with a communication in other circumstances that may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the matter is a programme in relation to a broadcasting service` MEANS
    (NOT `it is wholly related to or connected with a communication between 2 or more persons that is of a private or domestic nature`)
    AND (NOT `it is wholly related to or connected with an internal communication of a business, Government agency or other organisation for the purpose of its operation`)
    AND (NOT `it is wholly related to or connected with a communication in other circumstances that may be prescribed`)
    AND (`its primary purpose is to entertain, educate or inform all or part of the public` OR `it is advertising or sponsorship matter, whether or not of a commercial kind`)

-- src:515 | “provider”, for an online communication service, has the
-- src:516 | meaning given by section 2D;
@ref s 2(1) "provider" (src:515-516)
-- The meaning is in s 2D; the function is the same rule.
GIVEN `the entity is the provider under section 2D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the entity is the provider of the online communication service as section 2D gives the meaning` MEANS
    `the entity is the provider under section 2D`

-- src:520 | “regulated online communication service” means an online
-- src:521 | communication service that is designated under
-- src:522 | section 45K(1) as a regulated online communication service;
@ref s 2(1) "regulated online communication service" (src:520-522)
GIVEN `it is an online communication service designated under section 45K(1) as a regulated online communication service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is a regulated online communication service` MEANS
    `it is an online communication service designated under section 45K(1) as a regulated online communication service`

-- src:526 | “regulations” means regulations made under this Act;
@ref s 2(1) "regulations" (src:526)
GIVEN `they are regulations made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the instrument is regulations` MEANS
    `they are regulations made under this Act`

-- src:528 | “securities”, in relation to a company, includes shares,
-- src:529 | debentures, bonds and other securities of the company,
-- src:530 | whether or not constituting a charge on the assets of the
-- src:531 | company;
@ref s 2(1) "securities" (src:528-531)
GIVEN `it is a share, debenture, bond or other security of the company, whether or not constituting a charge on the assets of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) securities in relation to a company include this security` MEANS
    IF `it is a share, debenture, bond or other security of the company, whether or not constituting a charge on the assets of the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:533 | “shares”, in relation to a company, means shares in, or stock
-- src:534 | forming part of, the capital of the company;
@ref s 2(1) "shares" (src:533-534)
GIVEN `it is a share in, or stock forming part of, the capital of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the thing is shares in relation to the company` MEANS
    `it is a share in, or stock forming part of, the capital of the company`

-- src:536 | “Singapore end-user”, in relation to an online communication
-- src:537 | service, means any of the following end-users of the service:
-- src:539 | (a) an individual physically present in Singapore;
-- src:541 | (b) an entity which —
-- src:543 | (i) is incorporated under any written law; or
-- src:545 | (ii) is constituted or organised under a law of a
-- src:546 | foreign country or territory but registered under
-- src:547 | any written law;
@ref s 2(1) "Singapore end-user" (src:536-547)
GIVEN `it is an end-user of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an individual physically present in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an entity incorporated under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an entity constituted or organised under a law of a foreign country or territory but registered under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the end-user is a Singapore end-user of the service` MEANS
    `it is an end-user of the service` AND (`it is an individual physically present in Singapore` OR `it is an entity incorporated under any written law` OR `it is an entity constituted or organised under a law of a foreign country or territory but registered under any written law`)

-- src:551 | “social media service” has the meaning given by section 45T;
@ref s 2(1) "social media service" (src:551)
-- The meaning is in s 45T (module sgba-p10a-meanings.l4); here the result of that rule is a fact.
GIVEN `the service is a social media service as section 45T defines it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is a social media service as section 45T gives the meaning` MEANS
    `the service is a social media service as section 45T defines it`

-- src:555 | “subscription broadcasting service” means a licensable
-- src:556 | broadcasting service made available to the audience for
-- src:557 | whom it is intended only upon the payment of a subscription
-- src:558 | fee;
@ref s 2(1) "subscription broadcasting service" (src:555-558)
GIVEN `it is a licensable broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made available to the audience for whom it is intended only upon the payment of a subscription fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the service is a subscription broadcasting service` MEANS
    `it is a licensable broadcasting service` AND `it is made available to the audience for whom it is intended only upon the payment of a subscription fee`

-- src:563 | “subscription fee” means any form of consideration.
@ref s 2(1) "subscription fee" (src:563)
-- "any form of consideration": so any consideration at all makes it a fee.
GIVEN `any form of consideration is given for the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the consideration is a subscription fee` MEANS
    `any form of consideration is given for the service`
